WEBVTT

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.656
especially for TEDx in Amsterdam.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.016
So here it is.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:05.456
It's the same thing
as you can see over there --

00:12:05.480 --> 00:12:07.096
just 200 times bigger.

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.456
And I will very quickly
show you how it works.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.336
So just to explain.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:18.560
Now, every LED that is made
these days gives blue light.

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:22.776
Now, this is not very pleasant
and comfortable.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:29.696
And for that reason,
we cover the LED with a phosphor cap.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.416
And the phosphor is excited by the blue